NEST GAP #1: nothing currently PARSES .glsl/.hlsl/.vert/.frag source - there is no tree-sitter grammar for either wired into tools.behavior_tools, and shader code embedded as a C string literal is invisible to the C AST (a string is just a string to tree-sitter-c). HONEST GAP #2 (why these are NOT under `languages.c` like every other category): almost every one of these names (pow, clamp, length, distance, mix, dot, mul) is also a completely ordinary, extremely common C/C++ identifier unrelated to shaders (`pow` is literally libc\'s math.h function) - putting them in the real "c" lookup that scan_c_behavior uses would mislabel ordinary math/utility code as shader code. Deliberately filed under a separate `glsl_hlsl` language key instead, inert until a real GLSL/HLSL-aware scanner exists to use it correctly.\n',languages:{c:["texture","texture2D","texture3D","textureCube","texture2DProj","texture2DLod","textureCubeLod","textureLod","textureOffset","textureProj","textureGrad","textureSize","textureQueryLod","textureGather","texelFetch","imageLoad","imageStore","imageSize","imageAtomicAdd","imageAtomicMin","imageAtomicMax","imageAtomicAnd","imageAtomicOr","imageAtomicXor","imageAtomicExchange","imageAtomicCompSwap","atomicAdd","atomicMin","atomicMax","atomicAnd","atomicOr","atomicXor","atomicExchange","atomicCompSwap","atomicCounter","atomicCounterIncrement","atomicCounterDecrement","barrier","memoryBarrier","memoryBarrierShared","memoryBarrierBuffer","memoryBarrierImage","groupMemoryBarrier","EmitVertex","EndPrimitive","EmitStreamVertex","EndStreamPrimitive","dFdx","dFdy","dFdxFine","dFdyFine","fwidth","interpolateAtCentroid","interpolateAtSample","interpolateAtOffset","subpassLoad","mix","smoothstep","step","clamp","min","max","abs","sign","floor","ceil","fract","mod","modf","round","roundEven","trunc","sqrt","inversesqrt","pow","exp","exp2","log","log2","sin","cos","tan","asin","acos","atan","sinh","cosh","tanh","length","distance","dot","cross","normalize","facefor